{
  "description": "One pane for the fleet's billed model calls: the fleet-reliability SLO with its hits/errors inputs, traffic and latency by service, and LLM Obs cost/tokens by ml_app and by model. Seven apps in service plus two dormant RC1-322 smoke-test leftovers. The LLM Obs half filters on $ml_app and the APM half on $service — they cover different populations; see the header note. Hand-created (RC1-346). Cost metrics are nanodollars: formulas divide by 1e9 and pin the unit, because Datadog's own nanodollar metadata would otherwise apply the conversion twice (RC1-405).",
  "id": "bwm-uny-qqs",
  "layout_type": "ordered",
  "notify_list": null,
  "reflow_type": "fixed",
  "restricted_roles": [],
  "template_variables": [
    {
      "available_values": [],
      "default": "*",
      "name": "ml_app",
      "prefix": "ml_app"
    },
    {
      "available_values": [],
      "default": "*",
      "name": "service",
      "prefix": "service"
    }
  ],
  "title": "Agent Fleet — LLM Observability",
  "widgets": [
    {
      "definition": {
        "background_color": "transparent",
        "content": "Every billed Anthropic call the fleet reports, as traffic, latency, cost and tokens.\n\n**Seven apps in service** — **pr-review-agent** (94% of fleet spend) · **launch-planner** · **drift-digest** · **tpm-platform** · **kpi-agent** · **concert-intelligence** (RC1-362, spans hand-built in n8n) · **hihelloreid-chat** (RC1-361) — plus two dormant RC1-322 smoke-test leftovers, `agent-fleet` and `agent-evals-harness`, left visible on purpose: a filter that hid them would hide a future misconfigured app too.\n\n**The two halves of this pane cover different populations.** Cost, tokens and caching are LLM Observability and filter on `$ml_app` — the nine above. Reliability and Traffic & latency are APM `trace.anthropic.request`, which carries no ml_app tag, so they filter on `$service` instead. Two things follow, and neither is a bug: the **incident-summarizer Lambda** is in the SLO and in Traffic but in no cost widget (APM spans, no LLM Obs spans), and **`concert-intelligence` is the mirror image** — its spans go straight to the LLM Obs intake and never reach APM, so **the 97%/30d fleet SLO does not cover the concert workflow.** Say \"fleet\" with that in mind.\n\nDrill down in the [LLM Obs trace explorer](https://app.datadoghq.com/llm/traces). Per-case eval verdicts live on the case spans there, deliberately not charted here — gated-pass-rate on the [eval-run-store dashboard](https://app.datadoghq.com/dashboard/qz5-nmb-i9d) is their aggregate. RC1-322 · 324 · 339 · 346 · 405 · 406.",
        "font_size": "14",
        "has_padding": true,
        "show_tick": false,
        "text_align": "left",
        "type": "note"
      },
      "id": 5947308897804285,
      "layout": {
        "height": 2,
        "width": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
